  "reason": "The strongest unimodal evidence is RNA scvi_n200 multiprofile, with avgpool at 0.650 accuracy/0.628 F1 and transformer at 0.653/0.628, while the best tested image setting is imagenet_vit_l multiprofile avgpool at 0.332/0.315. This experiment tests whether adding that weak but tested image representation to the best RNA representation via simple concatenation can improve over RNA-only. It is the best next use of budget because it exploits the strongest RNA direction, uses a multimodal combination whose RNA and image subsettings both have unimodal baselines under the same profile/aggregation, and directly clarifies whether multimodality helps before spending experiments on fusion variants or untested image aggregations."
